clautolisp-tempprefix-empty — (getvar "TEMPPREFIX") returned "" on the mock host
================================================================================

Reported: pjb, 2026-07-30, while reviewing the pathname probe (the
probe's TEMPPREFIX fallback exposed it).

Symptom
-------

    $ clautolisp --host mock -x '(princ (getvar "TEMPPREFIX"))'
    (empty)

TEMPPREFIX ("Temporary prefix: the folder name for temporary files")
should never be empty. On a real CAD it is a registry-backed preference
(the Temporary Drawing File Location). clautolisp's mock host inherits
the AutoCAD-generated sysvar catalogue (sysvar-catalogue.lisp), where
TEMPPREFIX is a host-derived stand-in with default "", so GETVAR came
back empty and portable code that builds temp paths from it broke.

Expected (pjb)
--------------

- Default "/tmp/" on Unix, "C:/Temp/" on Windows.
- Stored / retrieved from the registry (vl-registry).
- Initialized from the TMPDIR environment variable (TEMP / TMP on
  Windows) when not already in the registry.

Resolution (clautolisp 1.7.4)
-----------------------------

New APPLY-TEMPPREFIX-DEFAULT in autolisp-cli/source/transmit.lisp,
called from INSTALL-TRANSMIT-VARIABLES at launch (the clautolisp-engine
path only — real CAD backends never call it, so a genuine CAD's
TEMPPREFIX is untouched). Resolution order:

    1. the value stored in the vl-registry
       (HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\clautolisp\Preferences / TempPrefix),
    2. else the environment (TMPDIR, then TEMP, then TMP),
    3. else the platform default ("/tmp/" | "C:/Temp/").

The value is normalized to a forward-slash directory ending in a slash;
a value resolved from the environment or the default is written back to
the registry so it persists like a real preference. Uses the HAL
generics host-registry-read / host-registry-write / host-set-derived-
sysvar (no mock-host coupling in the CLI layer).

Verified (clautolisp --host mock, SBCL)
---------------------------------------

    ;; fresh registry, no TMPDIR      -> platform default, persisted
    TEMPPREFIX=[/tmp/]                 ; registry now holds ("TempPrefix" . "/tmp/")
    ;; fresh registry, TMPDIR=/x/y     -> from the environment
    TEMPPREFIX=[/x/y/]
    ;; value already in the registry   -> registry wins, env ignored
    env TMPDIR=/ignored ... TEMPPREFIX=[/tmp/]

Note: a focused unit test was not added because autolisp-cli has no test
suite yet — clautolisp.asd's test-op for "clautolisp/autolisp-cli/tests"
references a system that has no defsystem and no tests/ directory (a
pre-existing gap; filed separately as a reminder). The behaviour is
covered end-to-end by the four CLI runs above.

CLOSED (clautolisp 1.7.4).
